WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.330
If you've been following the Blue Blur since
his debut in the early '90s, you probably

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.420
caught most of the Easter eggs in his feature
film debut.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.820
If you're a more casual fan, there are bound
to be a couple you missed.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.980
Just like Sonic himself, they go by pretty
fast.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:19.860
Before Sonic arrives on Earth, he lives in
a lush green paradise modeled after the first

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.360
level of his debut video game (more on that
in a moment).

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.770
Unfortunately, young Sonic's blissful existence
doesn't last long.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.150
It turns out that everybody wants Sonic's
super-speed, including a tribe of animals

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.370
that chase Sonic from his home planet to ours.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.020
Those aren't just any critters chasing Sonic
during the prologue, though.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.670
They're members of the Knuckles Clan, a tribe
of echidnas that originally appeared in Archie

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:45.810
Comics' record-busting Sonic the Hedgehog
line.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:50.430
The most popular member of the clan to us
is Sonic's ally Knuckles, who was named after

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.430
the tribe.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:55.151
Clearly, the Sonic the Hedgehog movie's take
on the Knuckles Clan is a little different

00:00:55.151 --> 00:00:58.329
from the comics lore, but it's still cool
to see them pop up.

00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:01.630
If they lead to an appearance by Knuckles
himself in the sequel?

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:02.630
Even better.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:05.170
"What you really need is some serious muscle."

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.800
"You mean me, right?"

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.800
“Right."

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.970
Most of Sonic the Hedgehog takes place in
a sleepy Montana town called Green Hills,

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.540
which was established in 1981, just a couple
of years before Sega released its very first

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.110
video game console.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:23.761
Nothing much happens there, at least not until
the little blue alien who calls Green Hills

00:01:23.761 --> 00:01:27.510
home gets angry and attracts the government's
attention.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:31.600
Green Hills is an appropriate place for Sonic's
adventure to start, given that it's named

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.830
after the first level in the inaugural Sonic
the Hedgehog video game.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:41.970
When Genesis owners booted up Sonic the Hedgehog
in 1991, Green Hill Zone was the first location

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.509
that players visited.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:48.240
Since then, Green Hill Zone's grassy slopes,
angular palm trees, and unstable cliffs have

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.009
gone on to become some of the franchise's
most recognizable sights.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:57.060
Since Sonic the Hedgehog, the Green Hill Zone
has reappeared in Sonic Adventure 2, Sonic

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.979
Forces, Sonic Mania, Sonic Generations, Super
Smash Bros., and plenty of other games.

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:06.369
You can even build a papercraft version of
the Green Hill Zone, if you want.

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:10.729
The Green Hill Zone is one of the most famous
levels in all of gaming, and it's a good thing

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:11.729
it's in the movie.

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:14.450
It just wouldn't be Sonic without it.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.560
Sonic the Hedgehog has a large and extremely
dedicated fanbase that loves to express itself.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.310
Unfortunately, fans' abilities don't always
live up to their passion.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:27.590
Spend a few minutes browsing DeviantArt, and
you'll see what we mean.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.510
There's an upside, though: As terrible as
some Sonic fan art is, though, it's a great

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:36.080
source of memes, some of which have become
just as famous as Sonic himself.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.300
Even the official Sonic the Hedgehog Twitter
account has gotten in on the fun, and naturally

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.030
the movie does as well.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:47.410
Early in the film, Green Hills' resident kook,
Crazy Carl, shows off a crude rendering of

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.700
the "Blue Devil," a not-so-mythical creature
that only Carl knows exists.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.650
Well, if you've spent any time on the internet,
you'll recognize Carl's drawing immediately.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:02.720
It's a very close recreation of the infamous
"Sanic Hedgehog," the star of a surreal YouTube

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.239
video who started as a nightmarish picture
of Sonic and has become a character all of

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:08.239
his own.

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:13.781
Later, when Sonic wakes up from a Robotnik-induced
stupor, he exclaims "Gotta go fast!" before

00:03:13.781 --> 00:03:17.200
racing all over a suburban San Francisco home.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.989
That's also a meme.

00:03:18.989 --> 00:03:23.940
In 2008, an endearingly awful drawing of Sonic
adorned with the phrase "Gotta go fast!",

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.950
which originated in Sonic X's title theme,
appeared on the fan site Sonic Central.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:34.590
Ever since, "Gotta go fast!" has been a rallying
cry for fans of bad fan art, and often appears

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:39.800
on parodies mimicking the original drawing's
weird, blobby "hedgehog."

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:45.680
Back in the days when Genesis did what Nintendon't,
every kid knew that Sonic was way cooler than

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:46.680
Mario.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.740
Just look at the evidence.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:52.420
Sonic could move much faster than Nintendo's
fat, lazy plumber, supposedly thanks to the

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:57.870
Genesis' much-hyped (and mostly bogus) "blast
processing" capabilities.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.720
Not only that, but Sonic had '90s-style attitude
to spare.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:06.099
When you booted up Sonic the Hedgehog, the
title character greeted you with a cocky grin.

00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:10.650
If you left him standing in one place for
too long, he'd tap his foot, shoot you a dirty

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.629
look, and in Sonic the Hedgehog 2 and later
titles impatiently check his watch.

00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:20.259
Sonic's irreverent idle animation has become
suitably iconic, and while Ben Schwartz's

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:25.249
big-screen version of the character isn't
as cocky as his 16-bit iteration, he's just

00:04:25.249 --> 00:04:26.249
as impatient.

00:04:26.249 --> 00:04:31.369
Near the end of the movie, when Sonic is facing
down Jim Carrey's Dr. Robotnik, the manic

00:04:31.369 --> 00:04:34.610
scientist launches a flurry of rockets at
the furry hero.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:39.849
Except, to someone who moves as fast as Sonic,
an attack like that is no problem.

00:04:39.849 --> 00:04:43.900
As he waits for the rockets to hit, Sonic
taps his foot and checks his watch, exactly

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.410
like he does in the game, before leaping into
action.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:53.469
You might know him best as Dr. Ivo Robotnik,
but in Japan, Sonic's archnemesis was originally

00:04:53.469 --> 00:04:54.889
called Eggman.

00:04:54.889 --> 00:05:00.050
In fact, as Takashi Iizuka, the head of Sega's
Sonic Team, tells Game Informer, that's what

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.180
the people behind Sonic's video games still
call him.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.870
As Iizuka tells the story, Sega of America
changed the character's name while localizing

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.999
Sonic the Hedgehog without consulting the
character's creators first.

00:05:11.999 --> 00:05:16.229
Unfortunately, when Sonic became popular,
the name Robotnik stuck.

00:05:16.229 --> 00:05:20.349
Eventually, frustrated by having to deal with
the villain's dual identity, Sonic Team decided

00:05:20.349 --> 00:05:25.669
to make "Ivo Robotnik" the villain's canonical
name, and Eggman his nickname.

00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:29.219
The mad scientist has been known by both monikers
ever since.

00:05:29.219 --> 00:05:32.369
"I just thought you might like a latte with
steamed Austrian goat milk."

00:05:32.369 --> 00:05:33.699
"Of course I want a latte.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.710
I love the way you make them!"

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:39.050
Sonic the Hedgehog also pays tribute to Eggman's
dual identity.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:44.349
As the movie nears its climax, Sonic mocks
Jim Carrey's Robotnik by nicknaming him Eggman,

00:05:44.349 --> 00:05:47.909
although he comes by the name a little differently
than the developers did.

00:05:47.909 --> 00:05:52.539
In the games, Robotnik is impossibly round,
giving him an egg-like appearance.

00:05:52.539 --> 00:05:58.340
In the film, Sonic has a habit of giving people
food-based nicknames just ask Tom "Donut Lord"

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:02.679
Wachowski if you don't believe us so when
he realizes that some of Robotnik's drones

00:06:02.679 --> 00:06:06.449
look like eggs, well, he really has no other
choice.

00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:11.789
In the video games, the main soldiers in Dr.
Robotnik's mechanical army are cyborg creatures

00:06:11.789 --> 00:06:13.659
known as Badniks.

00:06:13.659 --> 00:06:18.309
Powered by live animals, which they use like
batteries, the Badniks roam Sonic's homeworld

00:06:18.309 --> 00:06:23.309
searching for Chaos Emeralds, building superweapons
like the Death Egg, and doing everything they

00:06:23.309 --> 00:06:25.840
can to stop Sonic and his friends.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.740
Unfortunately, while Robotnik uses a number
of technological terrors to wage war on Sonic

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:34.780
and Tom, the Badniks don't appear in the Sonic
the Hedgehog movie.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:36.710
However, they could've.

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:39.089
Apparently, Robotnik has already made them.

00:06:39.089 --> 00:06:43.300
Later in the movie, when he's trying to harness
the power from Sonic's supercharged quill,

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.139
Robotnik accidentally shorts out his mobile
headquarters.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:50.560
When he opens the fusebox to restart the device,
we see a few different switches, each of which

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.779
are labelled with pieces of masking tape.

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:54.080
What does one of them say?

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.050
Why, "Badniks," of course.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.219
Okay, okay.

00:06:57.219 --> 00:07:02.220
There's only one way you missed this Easter
egg: You walked out of the theater as soon

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.649
as the end credits started.

00:07:03.649 --> 00:07:05.189
If so, shame on you.

00:07:05.189 --> 00:07:09.309
You missed the most crowd-pleasing moment
in the entire movie, not to mention the appearance

00:07:09.309 --> 00:07:12.509
of one of the most popular Sonic characters
of all time.

00:07:12.509 --> 00:07:13.900
Yes, that's right.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:18.529
After Sonic the Hedgehog's pixel art credits
sequence ends, none other than Sonic's number

00:07:18.529 --> 00:07:24.990
one sidekick and best friend (non-Tom edition),
Miles "Tails" Prower, makes his theatrical

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:26.139
debut.

00:07:26.139 --> 00:07:30.699
With a gust of wind, Tails appears out of
what seems to be another interplanetary portal.

00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:35.099
It turns out that Tails is searching for Sonic,
and while he's happy that the hedgehog is

00:07:35.099 --> 00:07:36.949
nearby, he's also worried.

00:07:36.949 --> 00:07:39.840
As he soars off into the distance, Tails mutters
to himself.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.169
Has he found Sonic too late?

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:43.319
Too late for what?

00:07:43.319 --> 00:07:46.550
Sadly, we don't know not yet, anyway.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:50.789
If Sonic the Hedgehog is a box office success,
the sequel should answer that question and

00:07:50.789 --> 00:07:52.900
put Tails front and center.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:53.900
Here's hoping.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.669
